    "created_at": "2016-11-17T16:38:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-17T16:38:13Z",
    "body": "Jaja. Didn't expect I'd have to put my own manhours where my mouth was. Before anything is done, I'd better look at existing front-end templates like Bootstrap.  I recall no serious built-in validations in this from a previous project but you never know. . . \nA JS library to resolve and restyle inputs on a form is fine. But this of course won't ever be automatic as it would need at least for the coder to add both a library link in the head and an onLoad=\"input-trans-lib.js\" property applied to the form. That's JS, of course. With jQuery it would be some kind of add-in with the option of opting out of it when desired. Just musing.\n",
